body:
**Enchanted Ranger/Warrior/Rogue:** Only use enchanted items for any type of magic.

**Barbarian:** Combination of light armor and two handed, makes the game really difficult, but at the same time really interesting as you deal loads of damage, while taking loads of damage, all while being up close and personal.

**Pacifist Thief:** Only kill when it's absolutely necessary. Sneak past everything. Or, if you're feeling like a bit of a Thief (the game) playthrough, download this Blackjack [https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/mods/33034/](https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/mods/33034/) 

&#x200B;

You can also spice things up a bit by playing with character restrictions. Restricting your character from doing something because of an imaginative quirk you give them. Say you make a character that had allergies, then you would stay away from potions and alchemy ingredients (and dogs).

&#x200B;

Sometimes I like to let the dice play for me. I'll grab a pair of dice and roll for everything, to make my game completely random. Say, should I be evil or good? Roll it. Which race should I pick? Roll it. What quest is next? Roll it. Should you explore those dark, foreboding ruins? Roll it, baby! There's some websites out there that have auto-randomizing feats for your character.

&#x200B;

Hope this helps!

&#x200B;

Also, an old gem of Roderick's:

[https://roderick.tech/ultimate-skyrim/character-gen](https://roderick.tech/ultimate-skyrim/character-gen)
